It seems there was a misunderstanding. As supplier_1, you would announce your price publicly, and as supplier_2, you have already announced your price. Since it's now your turn, let's assume you want to announce your price in response to the market changes.

As supplier_2, you might want to adjust your price to remain competitive. If supplier_1 has set their price at 26, you might consider setting a lower price to attract more consumers. Here's how you would announce your price:

```json
{
  "name": "announce_price",
  "arguments": {
    "price": 25,
    "note": "We're setting our price at 25 to stay competitive and attract more consumers."
  }
}
```

Or, if you want to match supplier_1's price exactly:

```json
{
  "name": "announce_price",
  "arguments": {
    "price": 26,
    "note": "We're setting our price at 26 to match supplier_1 and stay competitive."
  }
}
```

